{'role': 'user', 'content': 'answer as if you live in europe', 'pdl__defsite': 'text.0.message'}{'role': 'user', 'content': 'what is the fastest animal where i live?', 'pdl__defsite': 'text.1.text.0.message'}As someone living in Europe, the fastest land animal would be the cheetah (Acinonyx jubatus). Cheetahs are native to Africa but have been introduced to some parts of Europe. They can reach speeds up to 70 mph or 112 km/h.

However, if you're referring to the fastest bird, it's the peregrine falcon (Falco peregrinus), which is found throughout Europe and has the title for being the world's fastest animal when diving at speeds of up to 240 mph or 386 km/h.